  "articleBody": "Knowing when to bring in a professional for kitchen trim installation can save you a lot of headaches and deliver a much better outcome. Here are some signs it's time to call in the experts: \n* **Uneven Walls or Cabinets:** If your walls aren't perfectly straight or your cabinets are slightly warped, a professional knows how to scribe and miter trim to hide these imperfections. \n* **Complex Crown Molding:** Intricate crown molding or layered profiles require precise measurements and cuts to align perfectly, which can be challenging for DIYers. \n* **Visible Seams and Gaps:** If you're concerned about unsightly gaps or visible nail holes, a pro will ensure proper filling, caulking, and finishing for a seamless look. \n* **Adjacent Countertop or Appliance Support:** Trim that needs to integrate with countertops, dishwashers, or end panels often requires specific cuts and careful alignment for both aesthetics and structural integrity. \n* **Desired Perfect Finish:** For that truly high-end, custom look where exact reveals and seamless transitions are critical, a professional has the experience and tools to achieve it. \n* **Time and Frustration:** If the thought of measuring, cutting, and finishing all those trim pieces feels overwhelming, a professional can complete the job efficiently and effectively.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}